{"type": "message", "message": "**Minimalist means keeping what makes your home work, with less visual clutter—not leaving it empty.**\n\nFor a small flat, that usually means:\n- **A complete, restrained furniture set:** comfortable seating, a reachable table, good lighting and enough storage.\n- **Clear routes:** arrange furniture so moving between the entrance, rooms and balcony feels straightforward.\n- **Simple shapes and a limited palette:** warm whites, wood and a few coordinated colours rather than many competing finishes.\n- **Mostly closed storage:** everyday belongings stay accessible without every surface becoming a display.\n- **Warmth through texture:** fabric, a rug and personal favourites keep the space from feeling sterile.\n\nFor your combined living room and kitchen, I’d aim for one coherent seating area rather than scattered small pieces, while keeping balcony access clear. That’s a design direction—not a checked or applied layout yet.", "conversationId": "9f9932947e8045809aa7d0c9ec3bbf7d"}
